@page rh="THE HOUSE OF VANE · JUDAH · STANDING" m="TKC: CR · TL · MEN; VOL. I · {v1:crownward} · {v1:crown}"
# The public version and the private one
rec:
In public | He's been performing Judah Vane since before he understood what performing meant. The Temple formed him, the Crown trained him, and the Broadcast has filmed him since birth (CR).
The Crown Residence | Impeccably kept, and nowhere a person actually lives. He's never said so to anyone (CR).
The Study | A room on the Administrative Side, registered as a "policy research facility." Books not on the approved list, a window facing the Grace Bridge, no Broadcast equipment. The only place he isn't performing. His father, the Temple advisors and his own security detail don't know about it (CR).
What he suspects | The certainty he was handed was designed to keep him manageable more than to make him good. The Empire can't survive a Judah with genuine questions about the Empire (CR).
OPEN QUESTION | What does he know about Hannah, and since when (TL)?
prompt: What's on the Study's shelves | fill

@page rh="THE HOUSE OF VANE · JUDAH · FAITH AND SCRIPTURE · 1 OF 2" m="TKC: TL · CR; VOL. I · {v1:texts} · {v1:ledger} · {v1:prayer}"
# What he believes
rec:
Who taught him | The Temple raised him as much as his parents did (TL). The Prelate assessed his spiritual formation personally (CR). Temple advisors manage it still (CR).
What he believes | INFERENCE: Something he's been working out in the Study for four years that isn't Imperial (CR).
What he's looking for | The Covenant of Dissent, Elias's own counter-argument to everything the Empire was built on, written in the same hand the same year as the Covenant of Purpose (TL).
What he'd be arrested for, if he weren't the heir | The Study, the Grace Bridge, and a brother who's alive (CR, TL).
empire: What the Temple teaches about a man like him
The Vane bloodline carries God's anointing (CR). POSSIBLE: The Temple teaches him Genesis 49.10, "The sceptre shall not depart from Judah," as a verse about him.
/end
prompt: The question he's asked in the Study that he's never asked out loud | fill

@page rh="THE HOUSE OF VANE · JUDAH · FAITH AND SCRIPTURE · 2 OF 2" m="GEN 37.26–27; GEN 38.26; GEN 44.33; GEN 49.10; 1 KGS 19.4–12; DEUT 17.18–19; MARK 10.42–45"
# The text
rec:
Judah | Leah's fourth son. He proposes selling Joseph instead of killing him (Gen 37.26–27). He wrongs Tamar and admits it, "She hath been more righteous than I" (38.26). In Egypt he offers himself as a slave in Benjamin's place, the longest speech in Genesis (44.33, Vol. I, {v1:founders}).
Where Judah breaks | POSSIBLE: The biblical Judah sells a brother and later offers himself for another. Judah Vane inherited his brother's place and keeps his brother alive.
Elijah | Confronts a king and a queen, wins on Carmel, then runs, asks to die under a juniper tree, and hears God in "a still small voice" (1 Kgs 19.4, 12). The founder's name, Elias, is the King James New Testament spelling of the same prophet (Vol. I, {v1:cast}).
Where Elijah breaks | POSSIBLE: Elijah runs from the palace into the wilderness. Judah's wilderness is a room on the Administrative Side.
