@page rh="THE HOUSE OF VANE · JUDAH · VOICE" m="TKC: TR · WR 33–37"
# His voice
rec:
On the page | At the Pairing he sends the officials out, which has never been done. The Crown advisor resists, and he's "precise and final," and they go. He checks Eden for a wire and explains afterward what he did and why the order mattered (TR).
The exchange | "Most candidates tell me they feel called." "I know." (TR)
The rules | His early moves are small and deniable, a look, a barely-there nod, a shift near the door. He isn't a generic mysterious boy (WR 34, 36).
