@essay rh="THE HOUSE OF VANE · JUDAH · THE MACHINERY AROUND HIM"
# The machinery around him
drop: The Trials exist partly because of Judah's reluctance. The Empire needed a way to make his choice feel like honor and not pressure (MEN). An heir's Binding is the biggest Broadcast event of the year, and his staying unbound since twenty has become its own running story (CR).
He has rules on his side and none of them help. He can choose any of the twelve. "Without deviation" is a record and not a rule (FR 20). Deviation is permitted and expensive, and no heir has ever paid it (FR 21). If he refuses, the recommendation stands by default, so refusal is abstention and produces the same result as compliance (FR 22). The ranking tells him which choice is free.
His escape routes are a room nobody's traced and a bridge with a blind spot (CR), and a brother in Mountain Dominion who can't come back (TL).
side:
chips: MEN, CR, FR 20–22
k: Seven stages
stext: The Declaration, Covenant Week, the Anointing, the Binding Night, the Grand Binding, the Procession, the Private Supper (CR).
